    {
      "number": 2,
      "title": "Add caching support for IdentityProviderStorageProvider.getForLogin operations",
      "issue_comments": [{"body":"**Droid finished @varin-nair-factory's task** —— [View job](https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/actions/runs/21495336542)\n\n---","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:34:28Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/2#issuecomment-3820490373","id":3820490373}],
      "review_comments": [{"body":"[P1] Test cleanup uses hardcoded \"alias\" instead of created IDP alias\n\n`getCleanup().addCleanup(testRealm().identityProviders().get(\"alias\")::remove);` references an IDP literally named \"alias\" rather than the alias you just created in the loop. This leaves test data behind and can pollute subsequent runs. Use the actual alias variable/value (e.g., capture `final String idpAlias = \"idp-alias-\" + i;` and register cleanup with `get(idpAlias)::remove`).","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:40:27Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/2#discussion_r2743669933","id":2743669933,"line":381,"path":"testsuite/integration-arquillian/tests/base/src/test/java/org/keycloak/testsuite/organization/cache/OrganizationCacheTest.java","side":"RIGHT"},{"body":"[P1] Test cleanup uses hardcoded \"alias\" for newly created IDP\n\nAfter creating `idp-alias-20`, cleanup is registered with `get(\"alias\")::remove`, which won’t remove the created provider and can leak state between tests. Register cleanup with the actual alias string (\"idp-alias-20\") or a variable holding it.","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:40:33Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/2#discussion_r2743670272","id":2743670272,"line":425,"path":"testsuite/integration-arquillian/tests/base/src/test/java/org/keycloak/testsuite/organization/cache/OrganizationCacheTest.java","side":"RIGHT"}],
      "reviews": [{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/2#pullrequestreview-3657865900","id":3657865900,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-13T20:42:04Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/2#pullrequestreview-3672447675","id":3672447675,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-16T19:41:35Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/2#pullrequestreview-3693854134","id":3693854134,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T18:09:44Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/2#pullrequestreview-3694133482","id":3694133482,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T19:17:34Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/2#pullrequestreview-3708012483","id":3708012483,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-26T21:09:56Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/2#pullrequestreview-3712960383","id":3712960383,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-27T19:02:28Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/2#pullrequestreview-3714011471","id":3714011471,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T00:03:42Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/2#pullrequestreview-3718501721","id":3718501721,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T18:59:16Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/2#pullrequestreview-3725194773","id":3725194773,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:40:27Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/2#pullrequestreview-3725195115","id":3725195115,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:40:33Z"},{"body":"Caching for identity providers available on login looks sound and is covered by a new integration test, but the new test registers cleanup against a literal alias (\"alias\") instead of the created IDP aliases, which can leak state and make the suite flaky.","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/2#pullrequestreview-3725195273","id":3725195273,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:40:36Z"}]
