    {
      "number": 3,
      "title": "Add AuthzClientCryptoProvider for authorization client cryptographic operations",
      "issue_comments": [{"body":"**Droid finished @varin-nair-factory's task** —— [View job](https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/actions/runs/21495338066)\n\n---","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:34:32Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/3#issuecomment-3820490861","id":3820490861}],
      "review_comments": [{"body":"[P1] getBouncyCastleProvider() returns a non-BouncyCastle provider\n\n`getBouncyCastleProvider()` currently returns the Provider from the JVM default KeyStore (e.g., SunJSSE/SUN), not the BouncyCastle provider the interface contract implies. Callers expecting BC-specific behavior may misbehave or silently run with the wrong provider; consider returning the actual BC provider when present, or fail fast/explicitly (e.g., throw UnsupportedOperationException) if this minimal provider cannot supply it.","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:42:20Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/3#discussion_r2743676340","id":2743676340,"line":53,"path":"authz/client/src/main/java/org/keycloak/authorization/client/util/crypto/AuthzClientCryptoProvider.java","side":"RIGHT"},{"body":"[P1] Non-deterministic crypto provider selection when order() ties\n\n`detectProvider()` now sorts by `CryptoProvider.order()` only; if multiple providers report the same order, the chosen provider depends on ServiceLoader iteration/classpath order, which is not guaranteed to be stable. In this PR, DefaultCryptoProvider, WildFlyElytronProvider, and FIPS1402Provider all return 200, so environments with \u003e1 on the classpath can pick different providers across runs; add a deterministic tie-breaker (e.g., class name) or enforce/document unique order values.","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:42:20Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/3#discussion_r2743676341","id":2743676341,"line":55,"path":"common/src/main/java/org/keycloak/common/crypto/CryptoIntegration.java","side":"RIGHT"}],
      "reviews": [{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/3#pullrequestreview-3657865820","id":3657865820,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-13T20:42:03Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/3#pullrequestreview-3672445586","id":3672445586,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-16T19:41:10Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/3#pullrequestreview-3693852547","id":3693852547,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T18:09:16Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/3#pullrequestreview-3694156181","id":3694156181,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T19:20:48Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/3#pullrequestreview-3707991096","id":3707991096,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-26T21:04:43Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/3#pullrequestreview-3712960851","id":3712960851,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-27T19:02:36Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/3#pullrequestreview-3714033601","id":3714033601,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T00:15:40Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/3#pullrequestreview-3718539147","id":3718539147,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T19:04:47Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/3#pullrequestreview-3725201741","id":3725201741,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:42:19Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/3#pullrequestreview-3725201742","id":3725201742,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:42:19Z"},{"body":"Two correctness risks stand out: the authz-client CryptoProvider violates the `getBouncyCastleProvider()` contract by returning a non-BC provider, and provider auto-detection can become non-deterministic when multiple CryptoProviders share the same `order()`.","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/3#pullrequestreview-3725202227","id":3725202227,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:42:25Z"}]
