    {
      "number": 5,
      "title": "Add Client resource type and scopes to authorization schema",
      "issue_comments": [{"body":"**Droid finished @varin-nair-factory's task** —— [View job](https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/actions/runs/21495340842)\n\n---","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:36:15Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/5#issuecomment-3820500673","id":3820500673}],
      "review_comments": [{"body":"[P0] Potential NullPointerException when checking fallback permission\n\n`AdminPermissionsSchema.SCHEMA.getResourceTypeResource(...)` can return `null`. If it does, the subsequent `findByResource(server, resource)` call will dereference `resource` (e.g., `resource.getId()`) and throw a NullPointerException. Add a null check after loading the fallback resource and return `false` when it is null.","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:45:18Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/5#discussion_r2743687129","id":2743687129,"line":219,"path":"services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/services/resources/admin/permissions/ClientPermissionsV2.java","side":"RIGHT"}],
      "reviews": [{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/5#pullrequestreview-3657866886","id":3657866886,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-13T20:42:24Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/5#pullrequestreview-3672446527","id":3672446527,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-16T19:41:21Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/5#pullrequestreview-3693855169","id":3693855169,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T18:10:00Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/5#pullrequestreview-3694124674","id":3694124674,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T19:15:59Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/5#pullrequestreview-3708002288","id":3708002288,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-26T21:07:48Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/5#pullrequestreview-3712970952","id":3712970952,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-27T19:05:06Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/5#pullrequestreview-3714015471","id":3714015471,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T00:05:56Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/5#pullrequestreview-3718564279","id":3718564279,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T19:08:02Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/5#pullrequestreview-3725214279","id":3725214279,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:45:18Z"},{"body":"Found one concrete NPE risk in ClientPermissionsV2 when the fallback resource-type resource is missing; adding a null-check would prevent a crash. Other notes were either already addressed in the diff or were non-blocking cleanups.","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/5#pullrequestreview-3725214539","id":3725214539,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:45:22Z"}]
    }    ,
    {
      "number": 6,
      "title": "Add Groups resource type and scopes to authorization schema",
      "issue_comments": [{"body":"**Droid finished @varin-nair-factory's task** —— [View job](https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/actions/runs/21495342379)\n\n---","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:36:39Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/6#issuecomment-3820502063","id":3820502063}],
      "review_comments": [{"body":"[P1] Wrong identifier used for group permission evaluation and returned group IDs\n\nIn `getGroupIdsWithViewPermission()`, the loop uses `groupResource.getId()` (authorization resource internal id) both when calling `hasPermission(...)` and when adding to the returned `granted` set. But `hasPermission()` looks up the per-group resource via `resourceStore.findByName(server, groupId)`, where the resource **name** is the group id (see `AdminPermissionsSchema.resolveGroup()` returning `group.getId()`). Passing the internal resource id will miss the per-group resource, fall back to the all-groups resource, and also return the wrong identifiers. Use `groupResource.getName()` (group id) for the permission check and for the `granted` values.","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:43:31Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/6#discussion_r2743681002","id":2743681002,"line":123,"path":"services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/services/resources/admin/permissions/GroupPermissionsV2.java","side":"RIGHT"},{"body":"[P1] canManage() grants manage when only VIEW is present\n\n`canManage()` currently returns `hasPermission(null, VIEW, MANAGE)`, which makes VIEW sufficient to pass a manage check. That is a privilege escalation risk if callers treat `canManage()` as a write-authorization gate. Restrict the scope check to `MANAGE` (and any other write scopes intended), leaving VIEW-only users to pass `canView()` but not `canManage()`.","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:43:31Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/6#discussion_r2743681010","id":2743681010,"line":65,"path":"services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/services/resources/admin/permissions/GroupPermissionsV2.java","side":"RIGHT"}],
      "reviews": [{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/6#pullrequestreview-3657868362","id":3657868362,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-13T20:42:48Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/6#pullrequestreview-3672447693","id":3672447693,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-16T19:41:36Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/6#pullrequestreview-3693861190","id":3693861190,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T18:11:23Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/6#pullrequestreview-3694148760","id":3694148760,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T19:19:46Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/6#pullrequestreview-3707991039","id":3707991039,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-26T21:04:41Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/6#pullrequestreview-3712984398","id":3712984398,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-27T19:07:33Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/6#pullrequestreview-3714017769","id":3714017769,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T00:07:03Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/6#pullrequestreview-3718545129","id":3718545129,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T19:05:38Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/6#pullrequestreview-3725207229","id":3725207229,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:43:31Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/6#pullrequestreview-3725207239","id":3725207239,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:43:31Z"},{"body":"Two concrete authz correctness issues in `GroupPermissionsV2`: `getGroupIdsWithViewPermission()` appears to use the authorization resource internal id instead of the group id (resource name), and `canManage()` currently treats VIEW as sufficient for manage checks. Both can lead to incorrect access decisions.","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/6#pullrequestreview-3725207719","id":3725207719,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:43:37Z"}]
