    {
      "number": 7,
      "title": "Add HTML sanitizer for translated message resources",
      "issue_comments": [{"body":"**Droid finished @varin-nair-factory's task** —— [View job](https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/actions/runs/21495343696)\n\n---","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:37:05Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/7#issuecomment-3820503464","id":3820503464}],
      "review_comments": [{"body":"[P1] Wrong language string in Lithuanian locale\n\n`totpStep1` is now Italian (\"Installa una delle seguenti applicazioni sul tuo cellulare:\") in the Lithuanian `messages_lt.properties`. This will surface the wrong language to lt users; it should be translated to Lithuanian (or restored to the prior Lithuanian text) while keeping the intended meaning.","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:50:07Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/7#discussion_r2743702342","id":2743702342,"line":101,"path":"themes/src/main/resources-community/theme/base/account/messages/messages_lt.properties","side":"RIGHT"},{"body":"[P2] zh_CN message contains Traditional Chinese characters\n\n`totpStep1` uses Traditional Chinese (e.g., \"手機\", \"應用程式\") inside the Simplified Chinese `messages_zh_CN.properties`. For the zh_CN locale this should be consistent Simplified Chinese (e.g., \"手机\", \"应用程序\").","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:50:07Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/7#discussion_r2743702343","id":2743702343,"line":112,"path":"themes/src/main/resources-community/theme/base/account/messages/messages_zh_CN.properties","side":"RIGHT"},{"body":"[P1] Possible StringIndexOutOfBoundsException when building diff snippet\n\nThe mismatch reporting tries to trim identical prefix/suffix and then prints `value.substring(start, value.length() - end)` and `sanitized.substring(start, sanitized.length() - end)`. If the matching prefix and suffix overlap (i.e., `start + end \u003e value.length()` or `\u003e sanitized.length()`), these substring bounds become invalid (e.g., `value=\"a\"`, `sanitized=\"aXa\"` leads to `value.substring(1, 0)`). Add a guard to cap `end` (or skip trimming) so `start \u003c= endIndex` for both strings before calling substring.","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:50:07Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/7#discussion_r2743702347","id":2743702347,"line":110,"path":"misc/theme-verifier/src/main/java/org/keycloak/themeverifier/VerifyMessageProperties.java","side":"RIGHT"}],
      "reviews": [{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/7#pullrequestreview-3657867089","id":3657867089,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-13T20:42:29Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/7#pullrequestreview-3672447561","id":3672447561,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-16T19:41:35Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/7#pullrequestreview-3693854284","id":3693854284,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T18:09:46Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/7#pullrequestreview-3694155360","id":3694155360,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T19:20:42Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/7#pullrequestreview-3708001194","id":3708001194,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-26T21:07:34Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/7#pullrequestreview-3712968343","id":3712968343,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-27T19:04:28Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/7#pullrequestreview-3714018980","id":3714018980,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T00:07:46Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/7#pullrequestreview-3718575008","id":3718575008,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T19:09:20Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/7#pullrequestreview-3725232716","id":3725232716,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:50:07Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/7#pullrequestreview-3725232719","id":3725232719,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:50:07Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/7#pullrequestreview-3725232723","id":3725232723,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:50:07Z"},{"body":"Found one verifier-runtime edge case that can throw while building the diff snippet (overlapping prefix/suffix trimming), plus two user-facing translation regressions (lt string is Italian; zh_CN string uses Traditional characters) that should be corrected.","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/7#pullrequestreview-3725233083","id":3725233083,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:50:11Z"}]
    }    ,
    {
      "number": 8,
      "title": "Implement access token context encoding framework",
      "issue_comments": [{"body":"**Droid finished @varin-nair-factory's task** —— [View job](https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/actions/runs/21495345778)\n\n---","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:39:45Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/8#issuecomment-3820522835","id":3820522835}],
      "review_comments": [{"body":"[P0] isAccessTokenId matcher rejects valid IDs (inverted check + wrong substring)\n\n`matchesSafely` currently returns false when the parsed grant shortcut equals the expected shortcut, and it extracts the shortcut with `substring(3, 5)`. Per the token ID format encoded in this PR (`[2-char session][2-char token][2-char grant]:\u003cuuid\u003e`), the grant shortcut is at indices 4-6 and the matcher should fail only when it does *not* match. Use `if (!items[0].substring(4, 6).equals(expectedGrantShortcut)) return false;` (and consider guarding `items[0].length() \u003e= 6` to avoid `StringIndexOutOfBoundsException`).","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:46:38Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/8#discussion_r2743691471","id":2743691471,"line":487,"path":"testsuite/integration-arquillian/tests/base/src/test/java/org/keycloak/testsuite/AssertEvents.java","side":"RIGHT"},{"body":"[P0] rawTokenId null check uses wrong variable\n\nIn the AccessTokenContext constructor, `Objects.requireNonNull(grantType, \"Null rawTokenId not allowed\")` mistakenly validates `grantType` a second time instead of `rawTokenId`. This allows a null raw token ID to slip through and will fail later when encoding/using the token ID; change it to `Objects.requireNonNull(rawTokenId, ...)` so invalid contexts are rejected at construction time.","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:46:43Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/8#discussion_r2743691736","id":2743691736,"line":72,"path":"services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/protocol/oidc/encode/AccessTokenContext.java","side":"RIGHT"}],
      "reviews": [{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/8#pullrequestreview-3657865980","id":3657865980,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-13T20:42:06Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/8#pullrequestreview-3672447012","id":3672447012,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-16T19:41:28Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/8#pullrequestreview-3693862721","id":3693862721,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T18:11:39Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/8#pullrequestreview-3694151866","id":3694151866,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T19:20:12Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/8#pullrequestreview-3708017026","id":3708017026,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-26T21:11:05Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/8#pullrequestreview-3712971212","id":3712971212,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-27T19:05:11Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/8#pullrequestreview-3714017614","id":3714017614,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T00:06:57Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/8#pullrequestreview-3718549061","id":3718549061,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T19:06:12Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/8#pullrequestreview-3725219270","id":3725219270,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:46:38Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/8#pullrequestreview-3725219594","id":3725219594,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:46:43Z"},{"body":"This PR introduces context-encoded access token IDs; the approach looks coherent, but there are two correctness issues: a copy/paste null-check bug in AccessTokenContext and a broken AssertEvents matcher that will incorrectly fail tests and can throw on short strings.","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/8#pullrequestreview-3725219873","id":3725219873,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:46:49Z"}]
    }    ,
    {
      "number": 9,
      "title": "Implement recovery key support for user storage providers",
      "issue_comments": [{"body":"**Droid finished @varin-nair-factory's task** —— [View job](https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/actions/runs/21495346683)\n\n---","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:41:06Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/9#issuecomment-3820533747","id":3820533747}],
      "review_comments": [{"body":"[P1] Unsafe Optional.get() can crash the auth page\n\n`RecoveryAuthnCodesUtils.getCredential(user)` returns an `Optional`, but the bean calls `credentialModelOpt.get()` (and `getNextRecoveryAuthnCode().get()`) without checking presence. If the recovery-codes credential is missing (or if there is no next code), this will throw `NoSuchElementException` while rendering the login step instead of producing a controlled error/challenge.","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:50:36Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/9#discussion_r2743703901","id":2743703901,"line":19,"path":"services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/forms/login/freemarker/model/RecoveryAuthnCodeInputLoginBean.java","side":"RIGHT"},{"body":"[P1] NullPointerException in getCredentials() when user is not in backing map\n\n`getCredentials()` assigns `var myUser = getMyUser(user);` and then dereferences `myUser.recoveryCodes` / `myUser.otp` without a null guard. If `getMyUser` returns null (user not present in the `users` map), this will NPE; other methods in this class explicitly check for null after fetching the user.","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:50:36Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/9#discussion_r2743703904","id":2743703904,"line":232,"path":"testsuite/integration-arquillian/servers/auth-server/services/testsuite-providers/src/main/java/org/keycloak/testsuite/federation/BackwardsCompatibilityUserStorage.java","side":"RIGHT"}],
      "reviews": [{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/9#pullrequestreview-3657871348","id":3657871348,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-13T20:43:34Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/9#pullrequestreview-3672447530","id":3672447530,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-16T19:41:34Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/9#pullrequestreview-3693857489","id":3693857489,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T18:10:33Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/9#pullrequestreview-3694169552","id":3694169552,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T19:22:37Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/9#pullrequestreview-3708011125","id":3708011125,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-26T21:09:28Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/9#pullrequestreview-3712970887","id":3712970887,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-27T19:05:05Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/9#pullrequestreview-3714023692","id":3714023692,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T00:10:24Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/9#pullrequestreview-3718554628","id":3718554628,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T19:06:53Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/9#pullrequestreview-3725234503","id":3725234503,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:50:36Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/9#pullrequestreview-3725234507","id":3725234507,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:50:36Z"},{"body":"Two concrete error-handling gaps remain: an unsafe Optional.get() in the recovery-code login bean that can throw during page rendering, and a missing null guard in the test user-storage provider's getCredentials() that can NPE when the backing user entry is absent.","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/9#pullrequestreview-3725234901","id":3725234901,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:50:41Z"}]
    }    ,
    {
      "number": 10,
      "title": "Fix concurrent group access to prevent NullPointerException",
      "issue_comments": [{"body":"**Droid finished @varin-nair-factory's task** —— [View job](https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/actions/runs/21495348250)\n\n---","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:41:24Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/10#issuecomment-3820535874","id":3820535874}],
      "review_comments": [{"body":"[P1] Contract violation: getSubGroupsCount() can return null\n\n`GroupModel.getSubGroupsCount()` is documented to never return `null`, but this implementation returns `null` when `modelSupplier.get()` returns `null`. That violates the interface contract and can introduce NPEs in callers that rely on non-null. Consider following the existing adapter pattern and throwing `IllegalStateException(\"Not found in database\")` (as done by `getDelegateForUpdate()` / `isUpdated()`) or otherwise guaranteeing a non-null `Long`.","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:46:11Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/10#discussion_r2743689930","id":2743689930,"line":275,"path":"model/infinispan/src/main/java/org/keycloak/models/cache/infinispan/GroupAdapter.java","side":"RIGHT"},{"body":"[P1] Flaky test: spawned reader thread is never joined before asserting\n\nThe test starts a reader thread, sets `deletedAll` to true, and immediately asserts `caughtExceptions` is empty without waiting for the thread to finish. This can miss exceptions thrown after the assertion and can leak a live thread into subsequent tests. Store the thread in a variable and `join()` it (with a timeout) before asserting, and ensure the thread is stopped in a `finally` block so cleanup happens even if deletion fails.","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:46:14Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/10#discussion_r2743690150","id":2743690150,"line":148,"path":"tests/base/src/test/java/org/keycloak/tests/admin/group/GroupTest.java","side":"RIGHT"}],
      "reviews": [{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/10#pullrequestreview-3657867213","id":3657867213,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-13T20:42:31Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/10#pullrequestreview-3672447229","id":3672447229,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-16T19:41:32Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/10#pullrequestreview-3693861788","id":3693861788,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T18:11:30Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/10#pullrequestreview-3694150673","id":3694150673,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T19:20:03Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/10#pullrequestreview-3708007334","id":3708007334,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-26T21:08:45Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/10#pullrequestreview-3712971621","id":3712971621,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-27T19:05:18Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/10#pullrequestreview-3714019554","id":3714019554,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T00:08:04Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/10#pullrequestreview-3718551600","id":3718551600,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T19:06:30Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/10#pullrequestreview-3725217534","id":3725217534,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:46:11Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/10#pullrequestreview-3725217747","id":3725217747,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:46:14Z"},{"body":"Two concrete issues stand out: `GroupAdapter.getSubGroupsCount()` now violates the `GroupModel` non-null contract by returning null when the delegate disappears, and the new concurrency test can be flaky because it asserts without joining the reader thread. Addressing these will improve both runtime correctness and test reliability.","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-keycloak/pull/10#pullrequestreview-3725218060","id":3725218060,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:46:20Z"}]
    }
